      "title": "Centre redefines Ganga floodplain, drops ‘construction-free zone’ provision",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/centre-redefines-ganga-floodplain-drops-construction-free-zone-provision/article71335826.ece",
      "description": "The amendment removes the \"construction-free zone\" wording and instead says that the banks of the Ganga and its tributaries and their floodplains shall be maintained to reduce pollution sources and pressures, and preserve their natural groundwater recharge functions through necessary measures.",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-08-12T10:09:46"
    },
    {
      "title": "Govt redefines Ganga floodplain, drops 'construction-free zone' provision",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/govt-redefines-ganga-floodplain-drops-construction-free-zone-provision-126081200818_1.html",
      "description": "The Centre has redefined the \"active floodplain\" of the Ganga and its tributaries and introduced regulatory and warning zones based on flood return periods.\nThe Jal Shakti Ministry, through a notification issued on August 7 and published in the Gazette on August 10, has amended the River Ganga (Rejuvenation, Protection and Management) Authorities Order, 2016.\nThe latest amendment removes the \"construction free zone\" wording and instead says that the banks of the Ganga and its tributaries and their floodplains shall be maintained to reduce pollution sources and pressures, and preserve their natural groundwater recharge functions through necessary measures.\nAt the same time, the government has introduced a specific definition of \"active floodplain\", meaning an area of the Ganga or its tributaries coming under water due to floods corresponding to a one-in-five-year return period.\nThe amended definition of \"flood plain\" includes the active floodplain, a regulatory zone covering areas .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-12T07:55:57"
    }
  ]
